      "caption": "Before the Gate Opens\n\nIt takes a lot to build and support a two-acre camp for up to 100 people on the playa.\n\nBehind the scenes, it’s generators, a kitchen with 10 freezers and refrigerators, multiple grills, 40,000 watts of power, Shiftpods, bell tents, cots, air mattresses, 3,000 square feet of puzzle-mat flooring, 10,000 square feet of shade cloth, and the exoskeleton needed to hold it all up. Oh, and bikes! We own 30 of them, after discarding 15 last year that met their dusty fate! \n\nWe have a 20-foot toolbox for storing cables, audio gear, ratchet straps, anchors, and lighting, as well as a 20-foot kitchen trailer for housing kitchen goods. We also have box trailers for soft living goods like tents and AC units, and a huge trailer for hard goods like scaffolding and construction materials.\n\nThis year, it takes seven trailers, three diesel trucks, and three U-Haul trucks just to haul everything onto the playa.\n\nNot seen here: the pyramid being fabricated in China, or the geodesic dome currently buried under hundreds of pillows in the flatbed trailer.\n\nRight now, everything is being sorted, cleaned, repaired, and organized. Damaged equipment from last year’s windstorm is being discarded. Things we haven’t used in years are being donated to Habitat for Humanity. Everything that remains is being packed and stored so it can be pulled efficiently onto the playa the week before the gate opens.\n\nThis is the invisible part of building a city in the desert: months of preparation, maintenance, repairs, logistics, and care before anyone ever sees the lights come on, the shade go up, the kitchen start cooking, or the dance floor come alive.\n\nIt’s a massive undertaking, and somehow, every year, we do it again.",
