    {
      "caption": "🐘 Big news from Elephant Camp!\n\nPlacement has officially granted us the same location as last year—and even more space.\n\nThis year we’ll have 200 feet of frontage on Esplanade (up from 150 feet last year), along with additional camping space behind our frontage. Burning Man obviously highly values what our camp delivers! \n\nThe extra space means a more comfortable camp layout, more room for art, shade, and gathering areas, and less crowding throughout camp. RV campers may even have enough room to extend their own canopies and create private chill spaces, something that wasn’t always possible in previous years.\n\nWe’re still refining the final camp plan, but the possibilities are exciting. Now we just need to fill all that space with incredible people, creative energy, beautiful art, and a whole lot of Elephant Camp magic.\n\nIf you’ve been thinking about joining us this year, stay tuned—more details are coming soon. We have 20 unfilled spots, to reach our goal of 70 campers! We took in 110 people last year, so this year we are striving for greater intimacy, like years past!\n\nSee you on Esplanade!\n\n🐘✨",
